# THE LEDGER: what the toolchain does and weighs, one row a line. A row's KIND says how it is judged,
# and each kind is declared below by what keys it — what makes it deterministic — and how far it may
# rise (`wisp cost`). A count names no kind: the census compiler, cold, on each fixed workload of
# the pinned snapshot (`make cost`, tools/cost.sh), the same on every machine. A row only falls,
# through an accept; a new snapshot is `COST_SNAPSHOT=<sha> make cost-accept`.
kind bytes keyed-by toolchain over 0ppm
kind count keyed-by - over 500ppm
kind grows keyed-by toolchain over none
kind share keyed-by - over 0ppm+2000
kind speed keyed-by host over 250000ppm+250 least
kind told keyed-by - over none
kind wall keyed-by host over 0ppm
kind warm keyed-by host over 1000000ppm least
kind work keyed-by - over 0ppm
